  "scope": "Exact finer determinant quotient, common columns/group stage, division transport and selected D3 admission. GCF7-GCF11 have a separate independent review; eventual common realization remains explicit.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "topic": "Actual finer determinant quotient",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "Read GCF1-GCF6 and GCF12-GCF18. Hilbert-90 lifts are integral at almost every finite place, so they belong to the actual restricted product. The kernel, unit-image quotient and rational map are computed in KDq, not only in the ideal class quotient. The exact actual SG=(B.primes X).vGs is essential: it has no extra primes, and the selected paired congruence conditions are precisely the original ones."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Relative determinant and prescribed columns",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "The positive-part decorated ideal and determinant use the same given Reads frames and satisfy the full relative law in arbitrary rank. No globally free basis is assumed for self-dual lattices. The full columns extension preserves the supplied compatible group g. The actual element and object equalities are retained through the quotient and column constructions."
    },
    {
      "topic": "All group-compatibility fields on one tuple",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "Checked the canonical packC and gatOf tuple, using completed local isometry, self-duality, comparison, character and volume inputs at their exact scopes. The proof supplies the Hermitian and form fields, the whole CmpTied record, all four ring isomorphisms and five commuting identities, and GatIs. The exact IsRecG stores the same joint tuple. GCF7-GCF11, independently reviewed by main_proof_rigidity, supply the actual required period normalization."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Choice order and complete true-volume stage",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "Read the entire original exists_trueVolume_stage_of_any_column_choice. A single original GJStage is chosen before every later W,V,S,N. The stage-independent column and comparison maps, true-volume identity, original rational characters and normalized period supply VolTieG, GatNum and ColumnDataSplitPrimes on that same G. No per-later-stage choice has been substituted."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Division transport and actual comparison map",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "For arbitrary original submodules N and height functions h, the defining comparison polynomials and universal uniqueness give literal equality of the comparison map under setDiv. The full IsRecG and column-local-data records transport together; the period is unchanged. The four-component tuple in GCF17 includes the given Extra.cmp and kernel data, so an unrelated new comparison map cannot satisfy the conditional realization premise."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Selected tops and remaining common-family producer",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "The source ChosenE definition supplies ChosenTT and ChosenBad on the actual D3 family. The simultaneous threshold max{xa,xb,x1+1,(16*Cb+2)^(3/eps)} yields TopsF and the previously proved GLG16 gives Adm2F. Thus selected-top admission is not an additional producer on this selected class. The full class-level LinkG theorem still requires its original common realization or TSel, and GCF17 is conditional on the actual joint WPt realization. No GLOBAL_LOCAL_GAIN or other whole selected leaf is closed."
    }
  ],
